      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Holocaust",
      "label": "Holocaust",
      "description": "The systematic, state-sponsored persecution and murder of six million Jews by Nazi Germany and its collaborators during World War II. The meme falsely attributes a twisted justification to Hitler, implying he spared some victims to 'explain' his atrocities, which is historically inaccurate and deeply offensive. This requires background knowledge of the Holocaust to understand the gravity and falsity of the meme's claim.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_798b0878"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_287e1030",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Nazi_Germany",
      "label": "Nazi Germany",
      "description": "The totalitarian regime led by Adolf Hitler from 1933 to 1945, characterized by extreme nationalism, anti-Semitism, and the implementation of the Holocaust. The image of Hitler in a propagandistic pose is iconic of this regime, and the meme leverages this historical context to convey a hateful message. Understanding the political and social context of Nazi Germany is essential to comprehend the meme's offensive nature.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_798b0878"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1aa263d5",
      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Holocaust_denial_minimization",
      "label": "Holocaust denial/minimization themes",
      "description": "The false or distorted portrayal of the Holocaust as less severe, or the attempt to justify or rationalize the genocide. The meme's text 'i let some of them survive so you know why i killed them' is a grotesque example of this, implying a twisted moral justification for mass murder. This background knowledge is necessary to understand the meme's hateful intent and its attempt to trivialize historical atrocities.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
